        "# WordPress Studio Guide\r",
        "\r",
        "## Overview\r",
        "WordPress Studio is a local development environment for WordPress sites with an integrated AI assistant. As a relatively new tool (released approximately 2022), it has certain limitations that impact our workflow. This document outlines its capabilities, limitations, and its revised role in our development process.\r",
        "\r",
        "## Studio Assistant Capabilities\r",
        "\r",
        "### Informative Capabilities\r",
        "- **WordPress Development Guidance:**\r",
        "  - Provides code examples in PHP, CSS, and JavaScript following WordPress coding standards\r",
        "  - Offers best practices for security, optimization, and efficiency\r",
        "  - Suggests approaches for common WordPress development tasks\r",
        "\r",
        "- **WP-CLI Assistance:**\r",
        "  - Guides on using WP-CLI commands (pre-installed in Studio)\r",
        "  - Helps formulate complex WP-CLI operations\r",
        "\r",
        "- **Troubleshooting:**\r",
        "  - Helps diagnose and troubleshoot errors on local WordPress sites\r",
        "  - Provides solutions and guidance for common WordPress issues\r",
        "\r",
        "- **Documentation and Resources:**\r",
        "  - Links to relevant WordPress documentation and resources\r",
        "  - Offers contextual learning materials\r",
        "\r",
        "### Utility-Based Capabilities\r",
        "- **Site Management:**\r",
        "  - Create, manage, and configure local WordPress sites\r",
        "  - Assist with tasks like updating plugins, themes, and WordPress versions\r",
        "\r",
        "- **WP-CLI Execution:**\r",
        "  - Execute WP-CLI commands directly through the Studio interface\r",
        "  - Streamlines common WordPress management tasks\r",
        "\r",
        "- **Site Launch:**\r",
        "  - Guidance on launching local sites to production\r",
        "  - Support for the all-in-one-wp-migration plugin for site migration\r",
        "\r",
        "- **Contextual Assistance:**\r",
        "  - Has context about your specific site setup\r",
        "  - Tailors responses based on installed themes and plugins\r",
        "\r",
        "## Limitations and Challenges\r",
        "\r",
        "### Major Limitations\r",
        "- **Code Editing:** The Assistant cannot directly edit code on sites - it can only provide code snippets and guidance\r",
        "- **IDE Integration:** Studio does not currently have configured IDEs - code editing must be done outside Studio\r",
        "- **Version Control:** Limited native Git integration - requires external Git workflow (our current setup)\r",
        "- **Real-time Collaboration:** No built-in tools for team collaboration\r",
        "\r",
        "### Usability Issues (Added 2023-11-16)\r",
        "- **Performance Issues:** Slow loading times and poor responsiveness make development inefficient\r",
        "- **Editing Experience:** Lacks robust editing capabilities compared to wordpress.com's backend\r",
        "- **Interface Limitations:** UI/UX is still immature and lacks refinement\r",
        "- **Stability Concerns:** Being relatively new software (about 1 year old), it has stability issues\r",
        "- **Workflow Efficiency:** Creating a disjointed development experience requiring many workarounds\r",
        "\r",
        "## Revised Role in Our Workflow\r",
        "\r",
        "### PRIMARY WORKFLOW: WordPress.com Backend\r",
        "- Main development and testing now happens directly on wordpress.com (see wordpress-com-testing.md)\r",
        "- Use draft/preview mode for safe testing without publishing changes live\r",
        "- Leverage wordpress.com's mature tools and interfaces\r",
        "\r",
        "### SECONDARY ROLE: WordPress Studio\r",
        "- **Limited Local Development:**\r",
        "  - Used primarily for initial setup and occasional offline testing\r",
        "  - Useful when internet access is limited or for major structural changes\r",
        "  - For experimenting with configurations that might be risky online\r",
        "\r",
        "- **WP-CLI Tasks:**\r",
        "  - When command-line operations are needed that aren't available on wordpress.com\r",
        "  - Database exports/imports and other administrative tasks\r",
        "\r",
        "- **Emergency Backup:**\r",
        "  - Maintaining a local copy as a backup/failsafe\r",
        "\r",
        "## File Synchronization (Limited Usage)\r",
        "- Use our batch files only when necessary to sync code changes to Studio\r",
        "- Manual verification in WordPress admin after synchronization\r",
        "- Prefer direct wordpress.com backend editing for most changes\r",
        "\r",
        "## References\r",
        "- [WordPress Studio Official Documentation](https://wordpress.org/studio/)\r",
        "- [WP-CLI Documentation](https://wp-cli.org/)\r",
        "- [WordPress.com Testing Guidelines](wordpress-com-testing.md)\r",
        "- Internal docs: [sync-wordpress-files.bat](sync-wordpress-files.bat), [sync-assembler-quick.bat](sync-assembler-quick.bat)"
      ]
    }
  ],
